{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgHzQ9C45Z4eZG6tLFydB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing happens to it tomorrow. That's why I used a fixture.\n\nThe test writes its own temporary file with five known issues and passes that path to `weekly_report()`. It never reads `tracker.json`, so the hourly rewrite can't change the result. It will give the same answer tomorrow as it does today.\n\nA test that read the live `tracker.json` and expected 3 would break on the first sync that adds, closes, or reopens an issue. Nothing would be wrong in the code at that point. The test would be asserting a moving target.\n\nThe cost is that the test never reads the real file. If a sync changed the schema, for example renaming `state` to `status`, this test would still pass and the real report would break. A separate test could cover that. It would load the live `tracker.json` and check only its shape: a list, with each item having a string `state`. It would not check the count. I haven't added it. Do you want it?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":427,"cache_read_input_tokens":39774,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":427},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3ceb686-9bc2-4e3e-832d-75752caf0c5e","uuid":"8f6726e9-8206-482e-a1ad-ff02949cbe23","timestamp":"2026-10-22T21:32:12.098Z","request_id":"req_011CgHzQ8xuuKqVYvyQoaaVw"}
